  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 102,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets have roughly doubled since August 2026 (F-04: ~600/month Jun-Jul to ~1180-1260/month Aug-Sep), and the best-supported mechanism in current evidence is that field manual-meter-read route completion for ~9200 accounts fell below target (0.88 vs 0.95, F-01) during the same period, driving estimate substitution that accounts for the 41% of disputed bills built on ESTIMATED reads (F-02). This mechanism does not explain the majority (59%) of disputed bills, which are on ACTUAL reads, leaving that larger segment's cause open pending further investigation (billing rule changes, AMI data quality, or genuine usage increase)."
 },
