  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled since August 2026 (F-04). For the 41% of disputed bills on ESTIMATED reads (1240/3025, F-02), the best-supported mechanism is that billing-import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 with no unit scaling (F-10), compares raw AMI register values against 12-month m3 history; v4.2-firmware meters (rollout June 2026) report values in 0.1 m3 units versus v3.x's m3 units (F-11), so BV-17 misclassifies valid, on-time v4.2 reads as high-consumption and rejects them (1184/1240 = 95.5%, F-09), forcing estimate substitution. This mechanism does not explain the remaining 59% of disputed bills (1785/3025) on ACTUAL reads, whose cause is still open."
